# Approval means Plan mode

If the user asks to list findings, wait for approval, not execute until they confirm, or otherwise review before changes, **switch to Plan mode immediately**. Do not ask them to switch.

Stay read-only until they explicitly approve (for example “yes,” “make it so,” “ship it,” or “execute the plan”).

Do not rephrase internallish copy into a slightly softer placement lecture. Delete the lecture.
